tle": "Kelly Kirschner posts $224K in first quarter, says he's ready to battle Sydney Gruters in CD 16", "source": "Florida Politics", "published": "2026-07-15T07:00:00+00:00", "url": "https://news.google.?oc=5"}], "model": {"prior_margin": -5.07, "prior_sd": 5.11, "poll_margin": 1.0, "poll_sd": 10.6, "poll_weight": 0.19, "fundamentals": {"margin": 0.66, "lean": -6.0, "environment": 8.1, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.44}, "rating_margin": -8.89, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.84, "baseline_margin": -3.93, "analyst_adjustment": -2.07, "key_factors": ["District leans Republican by six points and this is an open seat", "Gruters holds a large fundraising and outside-spending advantage with Trump's endorsement", "Most expert ratings call the race Likely R; markets price Democrats near 17%", "A single low-weight poll shows a tied race, and some local Republicans have crossed party lines to endorse Kirschner"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point Republican: an R+6 open seat, Gruters' roughly $1.1 million raised plus $1.6 million in outside support against Kirschner's $300K, and a Likely R consensus among raters with markets at 17% for Democrats. The lone poll showing a tie and GOP crossover endorsements justify some movement toward the center, but not enough to escape Likely R.", "watch": "Whether additional polling confirms the August tie, and whether the Republican crossover endorsements expand into a broader anti-Gruters coalition.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Vern Buchanan (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Vern Buchanan's retirement leaves this Sarasota-Bradenton district open, and the contest pits Democrat Kelly Kirschner against Trump-endorsed Republican Sydney Gruters, with an independent also on the ballot. The seat leans Republican by six points, and Gruters has dominated the money race, raising over $1 million and benefiting from more than $1.6 million in outside support.\n\nKirschner has shown signs of life: a modest polling edge in one late-August survey and endorsements from several local Republican officials breaking with their party. Still, expert raters overwhelmingly call the race Likely R, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a one-in-six chance. The fundamentals and resource gap favor Gruters, with Kirschner needing a strong closing argument to close the distance.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.257, "margin": -3.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2349, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1906, "margin": -6.0}]}